{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43156 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Jionoside D appears to be a potent inhibitor of CD276 antigen through a multi-step mechanism involving microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein is targeted by Jionoside D and, in turn, is a target of other compounds, including 4-fluorobenzoic acid, which also leads to CD276 antigen targeting. The evidence suggests that Jionoside D may exert its effect by modulating the expression or activity of microtubule-associated proteins, which in turn influence the CD276 antigen. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CD276 antigen through different intermediates indicates a potential role for microtubule-associated proteins in the regulation of CD276 antigen expression. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Jionoside D interacts with microtubule-associated proteins to affect CD276 antigen remains to be fully elucidated.",
